  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The discriminant of the equation \\((-2 \\sqrt{2})^2-4(1)(1)=8-4=4 > 0\\) and \\(a\\) perfect square, so roots are real and different but we can't say that roots are rational because coefficients are not rational therefore.\n\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2 \\sqrt{2} \\pm \\sqrt{(2 \\sqrt{2})^2-4}}}{2}=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\pm 2}{2}=\\sqrt{2} \\pm 1\\)\nthis is irrational \\(\\therefore\\) the roots are real and different.",
